"Let $M$ be a binary matroid, let $T_M(x,y)$ denote its Tutte polynomial, and let $z$ be an integer. **Las Vergnas's second conjecture.** The value\n\n$$\n\\frac{T_M(-1+4z,-1+4z)}{T_M(-1,-1)}\n$$\n\nis an odd integer for every binary matroid $M$ and every integer $z$. This conjecture is the second of three conjectures made by Michel Las Vergnas concerning evaluations of the Tutte polynomial of binary matroids; it is stronger than the first conjecture and weaker than the third. The first conjecture was proved, while the third was disproved; this second conjecture is presented here as the subject of counterexamples."